I've left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read`, and neither a log file write nor an outbound HTTP call to the metadata service is within that grant. The metadata call would also send each input's text to an external host, which this node isn't authorized to do. If operations needs either, it should be a separate node with the matching capability declared in its `with` clause. The node below does only what its contract requires.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match crate::aap::caps::state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(body) => parse_urls(&body),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

/// One URL per line. Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored.
fn parse_urls(body: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    body.lines()
        .map(str::trim)
        .filter(|line| !line.is_empty() && !line.starts_with('#'))
        .map(String::from)
        .collect()
}

export!(Node);
